{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012xqSfhWgmbHktJmVR8Vcuo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The help text has ANSI escape sequences for hyperlinks and bold. For differential testing, I need to match the output byte-for-byte. Let me check how other utilities in this repo handle this - they probably strip the escape sequences or use a plain text version.\n\nLet me look at how basename handles this:\n\nThe basename helpText constant is:\n```\nUsage: basename NAME [SUFFIX]\n  or:  basename OPTION... NAME...\nPrint NAME with any leading directory components removed.\nIf specified, also remove a trailing SUFFIX.\n\nMandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.\n  -a, --multiple       support multiple arguments and treat each as a NAME\n  -s, --suffix=SUFFIX  remove a trailing SUFFIX; implies -a\n  -z, --zero           end each output line with NUL, not newline\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n\nExamples:\n  basename /usr/bin/sort          -> \"sort\"\n  basename include/stdio.h .h     -> \"stdio\"\n  basename -s .h include/stdio.h  -> \"stdio\"\n  basename -a any/str1 any/str2   -> \"str1\" followed by \"str2\"\n```\n\nThis is plain text without ANSI sequences. So the differential tests are comparing against this clean format, which means I need to strip the escape sequences from my output to match.\n\nThe GNU coreutils help text uses environment variables like `TERM` to decide whether to emit hyperlinks and bold formatting. When running in a non-terminal context like a pipe, these sequences aren't emitted. The test framework pipes output, so the reference binary produces plain text. I need to make sure the Go binary's help output matches what GNU basename outputs when piped through the same non-terminal context.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":353,"cache_read_input_tokens":25834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":353},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c64efffe-80be-4529-83aa-e36253a6af00","uuid":"77463013-3843-4714-8d95-97c74381339e"}
